/**
 * @file mainpage.dox
 *
 * @mainpage Foundation Documentation
 *
 * @brief Documentation for the Foundation framework.
 *
 * Foundation is a modular C++ framework for embedded and desktop
 * software development.
 *
 * It provides reusable, lightweight components intended to serve as a
 * common base layer for embedded applications, desktop tools, and
 * higher-level frameworks.
 *
 * @section MainPage_Overview Overview
 *
 * Foundation is organized into independent modules. Each module focuses
 * on a specific domain and may be enabled or disabled through the build
 * system.
 *
 * Main framework topic:
 *
 * - @ref Foundation
 *
 * @section MainPage_PublicApi Public API
 *
 * Application code should normally include Foundation through its
 * top-level public headers.
 *
 * Main public API page:
 *
 * - @ref FoundationTopLevelHeaders
 *
 * Common include styles:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include <Foundation.h>
 * @endcode
 *
 * or:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include <Foundation_Math.h>
 * #include <Foundation_Time.h>
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section MainPage_Modules Modules
 *
 * Foundation is divided into the following main modules:
 *
 * - @ref Foundation_TypeTraits
 * - @ref Foundation_Math
 * - @ref Foundation_Time
 * - @ref Foundation_Containers
 * - @ref Foundation_Functional
 * - @ref Foundation_Scheduling
 * - @ref Foundation_Utils
 *
 * @section MainPage_GettingStarted Getting Started
 *
 * For small applications, examples, and Arduino-style projects, include
 * the main header:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include <Foundation.h>
 * @endcode
 *
 * For larger projects or library code, prefer selective module headers:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include <Foundation_Math.h>
 * #include <Foundation_Time.h>
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section MainPage_Build Build and Installation
 *
 * Foundation uses CMake as its primary build system.
 *
 * Build documentation:
 *
 * - @ref Foundation_BuildGuide
 * - @ref Foundation_Workflows
 *
 * The build system supports:
 *
 * - Desktop builds.
 * - Documentation builds.
 * - Coverage builds.
 * - Embedded distributions.
 * - Precompiled library exports.
 *
 * @section MainPage_Examples Examples
 *
 * Example documentation is available here:
 *
 * - @ref Foundation_Examples
 *
 * Examples demonstrate how to use Foundation modules in practical
 * desktop and embedded scenarios.
 *
 * @section MainPage_RepositoryLayout Repository Layout
 *
 * The project is generally organized as:
 *
 * @code
 * Foundation/
 * ├── docs/
 * ├── src/
 * ├── examples/
 * ├── tests/
 * ├── scripts/
 * ├── CMakeLists.txt
 * └── CMakePresets.json
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section MainPage_DesignGoals Design Goals
 *
 * Foundation is designed with the following goals:
 *
 * - Embedded-first architecture.
 * - Desktop compatibility.
 * - Modular feature selection.
 * - Stable top-level public headers.
 * - Minimal runtime overhead.
 * - Minimal dependency on the C++ standard library.
 * - Clear separation between public API and internal implementation.
 *
 * @section MainPage_Platforms Supported Platforms
 *
 * Foundation is intended to support:
 *
 * - Windows
 * - Linux
 * - macOS
 * - Arduino-style environments
 * - AVR-GCC / ATmega328P
 * - PSoC Creator projects
 * - STM32 projects
 * - Other C++17-capable embedded targets
 *
 * @section MainPage_NextSteps Next Steps
 *
 * Recommended reading order:
 *
 * - @ref Foundation
 * - @ref FoundationTopLevelHeaders
 * - @ref Foundation_BuildGuide
 * - @ref Foundation_Workflows
 * - @ref Foundation_Workflows_Validation
 * - @ref Foundation_Examples
 * - Module documentation such as @ref Foundation_Math or @ref Foundation_Time
 */
